# Approved runtime hash of Valheim's live admin surface — adminlist.txt and
# permittedlist.txt hashed together as one blob (see manifest.json live_config).
#
# Both should be the image's stock comment-only files with NO SteamIDs in them.
# That is the whole point: an empty admin list is what makes this server fair.
#
# After your FIRST deploy (once the container has written /config), run:
#     python3 watcher/watcher.py --approve valheim
# then commit this file. The watcher and the off-host GitHub Action both compare
# the live files against this value — any drift raises an alert.
#
# Re-run --approve and commit again WHENEVER you legitimately change one (which
# for Valheim should be close to never — adding an admin is exactly the thing
# this repo exists to make impossible to do quietly).
# The first non-comment line below is read as the hash:
REPLACE_AFTER_FIRST_DEPLOY
